questions.explanation:
Section 48 fixes the order in which a dissolved firm applies its assets:
(i) debts of the firm to third parties;
(ii) partners' loans and advances, as distinguished from capital;
(iii) partners' capitals;
(iv) any residue, shared in the profit sharing ratio.
So a partner's loan is paid before any capital is returned. Option (1) is tempting, but capital comes only after partners' loans are cleared.
Answer: (2)
